WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.940
The lead-up to Star Wars Episode IX is proving
to be pretty exciting, and leading to plenty

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.260
of wild speculation.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.920
Strap on your helmets, nerf herders, you're
in for a bumpy ride as we explore some of

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.000
the latest spoilers and rumors from a galaxy
far, far away.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.780
Disney decided to clean house in a big way
ahead of The Force Awakens, declaring that

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.800
all Extended Universe materials were no longer
considered Star Wars canon.

00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:27.539
The Mouse House then set about creating its
own line of short stories, comics, and books

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:32.180
to tie in with the new continuity, and one
such release might just include a huge clue

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.240
about a major Episode IX character.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:40.080
In Poe Dameron #27, a conversation Poe has
with Rey and Finn seems to confirm that he's

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.160
been unwittingly channeling the Force all
this time.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.040
Marvel's Poe Dameron comics overlap with J.J.
Abrams' The Force Awakens.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.480
#26 explained how Dameron survived that crash
and filled us in on what he did between then

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:57.730
and rescuing Rey and Finn from the First Order,
but it was the following issue that really

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:58.940
got readers talking.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.500
In it, Dameron admits that he's been able
to tap into some kind of "energy" while flying,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.180
prompting both Rey and Leia to suggest he's
been using the Force.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:13.280
The seeds of this reveal were actually planted
in the 2015 series Star Wars: Shattered Empire,

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.100
according to CBR.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.580
It's in this prelude to The Force Awakens
that we learn how Luke Skywalker gave remnants

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.610
of The Great Tree, a natural conduit of the
Force, to Dameron's parents, who used them

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.180
to grow a new tree at home on Yavin 4.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.040
Dameron even mentions growing up around this
tree, further foreshadowing a connection to

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:31.700
the Force.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.360
You'll need to take this Rise of Skywalker
rumor with a generous sprinkling of Crait's

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:41.000
finest surface salt, because it originated
from an unverified source.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.500
According to The Sun, Ewan McGregor will return
as Obi-Wan Kenobi for the upcoming trilogy

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.220
closer, though Disney is reportedly keen to
keep that fact under wraps.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.590
McGregor portrayed Obi-Wan in Episodes I through
III and has already reprised the role in voiceover

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.440
form, speaking directly to Rey during a Force
vision in 2015's The Force Awakens.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.000
He recorded some brand new dialogue for his
brief audio cameo…

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.640
"Rey…These are your first steps."

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.160
…which was mixed with lines from preexisting
Star Wars movies.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.980
His voice was actually blended with that of
original Obi-Wan actor Alec Guinness, and

00:02:16.981 --> 00:02:21.230
more recent reports suggest that this approach
will be taken one step further in The Rise

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.120
of Skywalker.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:27.180
According to Star Wars enthusiast Mike Zeroh,
J.J. Abrams will return to the moment Obi-Wan

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.020
contacted Rey in The Force Awakens and flesh
it out somewhat.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:35.980
The late Jedi Master will reportedly appear
as a Force Ghost, his features altered to

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.800
somewhat resemble both McGregor and Guinness,
and offer Rey some much-needed guidance.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:46.760
Dominic Monaghan of Lost and Alias' Greg Grunberg
are both in The Rise of Skywalker, but they

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.040
aren't the only Abrams alumni appearing.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:54.540
Felicity star Keri Russell is also in Episode
IX, though she wasn't chosen simply because

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.760
she's part of the club.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.000
According to Variety's Justin Kroll, Russell's
experience made her the ideal choice.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:01.840
Kroll revealed:

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.520
"The role calls for action-heavy fight scenes.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.080
Russell has shown her ability to perform tough
stunts in projects like FX's The Americans,

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.200
Mission: Impossible, and Dawn of the Planet
of the Apes."

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.560
The name of Russell's character wasn't known
at the time, but subsequent leaks shed some

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.060
light.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.280
In March 2019, several merchandising images
appeared online, including one of a masked

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.530
woman named Zorri who appeared to be a new
bounty hunter.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.700
"Bounty hunters?

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.360
We don't need their scum."

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.820
Fan site Making Star Wars shared the leaked
pictures, explaining:

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.140
"The images give us a good look at Zorri.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.460
Based on what my sources have described to
me about Keri Russell's character, I can't

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.460
see how it isn't the same character."

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.260
Those sources, it appears, were dead on.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:48.760
It didn't explicitly refer to her as a bounty
hunter, but Vanity Fair released a hi-res

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:54.160
photo of Russell as, quote, "the masked scoundrel
Zorri Bliss" after being granted exclusive

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.220
behind-the-scenes access to Episode IX, seemingly
confirming the rumors.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:03.180
Bliss was shown on, quote, "the Thieves' Quarter
of the snow-dusted world Kijimi," one of two

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.020
new planets and a possible entry point for
Lando Calrissian.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:06.880
How big a part will Lando play?

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.420
For fans of the original trilogy, one of the
biggest moments in the first Episode IX teaser

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:15.500
trailer was seeing Lando Calrissian back in
the cockpit of the Millennium Falcon.

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:20.080
The Hollywood Reporter revealed that Billy
Dee Williams was reprising the role in July

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:25.410
2018, but details of Calrissian's part in
The Rise of Skywalker were kept under wraps

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.730
in the months that followed.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:31.000
Early rumors suggested that the charming smuggler
would be playing a significant role in the

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.420
saga closer, but that doesn't appear to be
the case.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.080
While his daughter is rumored to be making
an appearance, Calrissian himself isn't likely

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:43.140
to feature very prominently, because J.J.
Abrams has so much to squeeze in.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:48.650
Inverse predicts, quote, "Lando's screentime
in the movie will be on par with Admiral Ackbar's

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.580
short scenes in The Force Awakens."

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:56.020
Williams kept the details of Calrissian's
arc to himself at Star Wars Celebration 2019,

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.220
but he was happy to defend his character's
past actions.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.420
Of his divisive betrayal of Han Solo in The
Empire Strikes Back, Williams said:

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.320
"He was up against Darth Vader, he had to
figure out something.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.020
Besides, did anybody die?"

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:13.080
He makes a fair point, but this moment has
always been a bone of contention among fans.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:17.820
Could Calrissian, who will apparently wear
the same getup he wore when he first met Solo,

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.340
be out to avenge his death as a way of finally
making amends?

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.060
Episode IX will tie up a number of loose ends,
after all.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:29.640
One of the wildest Episode IX rumors, the
theory that Han Solo is alive, is partly backed

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.100
up by the novelization of The Force Awakens.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:36.750
The book was picked apart by Uproxx, and there's
a big reveal about the Starkiller Base that

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.700
has Harrison Ford fans speculating on an unlikely
return.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.700
The book explained what the movie didn't;
how the giant weapon is powered.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:50.120
The assumption was that it harnessed the power
of the sun, but the truth is far more complicated.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.270
Uproxx's Donna Dickens reports:

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.140
"Turns out, it was never supposed to be powered
by the sun.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.870
Situated in one place, messing with science
they didn't understand, the First Order was

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:02.120
harvesting dark matter to power their weapon.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.420
As the matter congealed to be sucked into
the core, the light was supposed to dim.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:10.880
Then, using more science they barely understood,
they beamed the concentrated dark matter through

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.980
the galaxy instead of across it.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.840
Basically, they were ripping holes in time/space."

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.280
Solo appeared to have been killed by his own
son when we saw him last, but there's now

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.820
a theoretical chance that he was sucked into
an alternate timeline before he bled out.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.360
One fan who's excited at the prospect is director
and Star Wars fanatic Kevin Smith, who tweeted:

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:35.040
"[If a plot development] allows Lando to repeat
his Empire Strikes Back line 'There's still

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.100
a chance to save Han!' and get us back to
that fateful bridge on Starkiller Base?

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.960
Then I'll kiss J.J. on the mouth."

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:46.380
Numerous disgruntled Star Wars fans made their
disapproval of Rian Johnson's The Last Jedi

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:50.850
known, but the one thing that everyone seemed
to agree was done right was the surprise appearance

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:51.600
from Yoda.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.051
The little green Jedi Master showed up as
a Force Ghost to help troubled former student

00:06:56.051 --> 00:07:01.070
Luke Skywalker come to his senses and embrace
his failures, a standout moment in the highly

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.560
divisive eighth episode.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:07.920
Yoda was rendered in CGI for the prequel trilogy,
but Johnson chose to go back to basics and

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.560
brought in Frank Oz to operate a slightly
updated Yoda puppet.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.560
Creature designer Neal Scanlan said:

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:17.760
"We just felt that it was absolutely right
and proper that we create the puppet in the

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.240
closest likeness to the original and to give
Frank exactly what he had the first time around."

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:27.180
Renowned puppeteer Oz, who provides Yoda's
distinctive voice as well as his movements,

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:31.780
could soon be adding Episode IX to his impressive
résumé if a new report is to be believed.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:36.100
According to the New York Daily News, a source
with apparent knowledge of the production

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.920
has revealed that J.J. Abrams is going to
bring Force Ghost Yoda back.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.340
The insider dished:

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:45.100
"The success of the scenes featuring Yoda
in The Last Jedi were huge.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:49.800
Yoda will again appear as a ghost as he acknowledges
Rey's success and growth as a Jedi."

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:55.340
Lucasfilm's original position on Carrie Fisher's
inclusion in future Star Wars movies was pretty

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:57.600
clear; she wouldn't be appearing in any.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:02.160
Prior to the release of The Last Jedi, President
Kathleen Kennedy told ABC:

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.840
"Sadly, Carrie will not be in [Episode] IX."

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:08.780
The idea that they could digitally render
a version of Fisher like they did with Peter

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:14.040
Cushing's Tarkin in Rogue One was quickly
ruled out after execs met with Fisher's daughter,

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:14.620
Billie Lourd.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.060
All parties reportedly agreed that it would
be disrespectful.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:23.000
At the time, bringing Leia back with unused
footage from The Last Jedi was also said to

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.760
have been off the table, but things have shifted
since then.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:30.740
We now have confirmation from the late actress'
brother that Fisher will indeed be in Episode

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:35.210
IX, with J.J. Abrams apparently set to use
footage shot for both The Last Jedi and The

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.380
Force Awakens.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:41.960
According to ABC's Clayton Sandell, who spoke
to Todd Fisher on podcast The Resistance Broadcast,

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:44.840
the family is very happy about what Abrams
has planned.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:49.300
Sandell claimed that Todd Fisher was, quote,
"very excited, the whole family is really

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.480
excited about this and wanted it to happen."

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.420
Sandell went on to explain:

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:57.460
"There are big surprises coming with this
movie and with this performance and with this

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.500
unused footage.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.280
This one's really for the fans…

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:04.851
Sandell confirmed that there's "a number of
minutes" worth of footage from The Force Awakens

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.100
and The Last Jedi for Abrams to work with.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:12.360
When ThatHashtagShow reported that Disney
wanted a female lead between the ages of 40

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:16.860
and 50 to play a character named Mara, many
jumped to the conclusion that this was Rey's

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:17.360
mother.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:21.920
The character does seem to fit the bill, but
now there's a fresh rumor about Rey's mom,

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:22.940
and it's a shocker.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.260
And before you say it, no, we seriously doubt
that Kylo's take on Rey's parents, that they

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:31.460
were nobodies who sold her for drinking money,
holds any water.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.000
According to the theory posed by Film Threat,
Episode IX will see Rey's real mom and dad

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.780
revealed to be none other than Han Solo and
Emilia Clarke's Qi'ra.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:44.480
We were introduced to Han's first love in
Solo: A Star Wars Story, a movie that could

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:47.490
apparently end up being all about Rey's parents.

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:49.540
Film Threat's prediction goes on to explain:

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:53.600
"Solo ended letting us know that Qi'ra has
ties to the Dark Side.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:56.940
Kylo Ren is the son of Leia, a mother of the
Light Side.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:00.950
Qi'ra, a mother of the Dark Side, bore a Light
Side daughter, Rey.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.420
It's the Force balancing itself."

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:07.360
Of course, if this theory turns out to be
accurate, that means Han cheated on Leia and

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:08.980
fathered a daughter with another woman.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.700
While this could actually explain a number
of things, such as why Kylo Ren resented his

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.100
dad so much and why he and Rey are connected
through the Force, not everyone is buying

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:18.600
it.

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:23.020
As ScreenRant points out, quote, "There's
been nothing to indicate Han was unfaithful

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:23.600
to Leia."

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:28.720
The idea of Darth Vader returning to the big
screen in Episode IX might seem ludicrous

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:33.210
on the surface, but Disney has been subtly
paving the way for the heavy-breathing Sith

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.940
Lord to play some part in the upcoming installment.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:41.120
After reading Marvel's Darth Vader comics,
ScreenRant noticed one small detail that could

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.480
have actually been a huge moment of foreshadowing.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:47.850
The ins and outs of becoming a Force Ghost
have been up for discussion among Star Wars

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:51.830
fans ever since Luke Skywalker passed on in
controversial fashion near the end of The

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:52.540
Last Jedi.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:57.160
The assumption was that returning as a Force
Ghost was something only those in tune with

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:00.980
the light side of the Force could do, but
shouldn't the Sith have their own version

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:02.060
of this phenomenon?

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:06.340
Turns out they do, and it was explained in
the pages of the Vader comic.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:10.760
In the story in question, Vader is gifted
a mask that once belonged to another powerful

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.380
Sith called Darth Momin.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:16.800
Momin's "residue" was still attached to the
artifact when Palpatine gave it to his third

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:21.960
and final apprentice, who used it, long story,
to help erect his castle on Mustafar.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:27.060
The forgotten Sith was able to influence others,
and tell his story to Vader, via the mask.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:31.500
ScreenRant's prediction is that Vader will
similarly influence proceedings in Episode

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:36.820
IX, seeing as his grandson Kylo Ren is now
in possession of Vader's half-melted mask.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:41.351
With appearances on Doctor Who and Game of
Thrones under his belt, veteran character

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:46.960
actor Richard E. Grant already had some major
fan cred when he was cast in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:50.420
As it turns out, he's a big Star Wars fanboy
himself.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:54.340
The actor opened up about the moment J.J.
Abrams told him he'd be part of the final

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:59.650
chapter in the Skywalker saga while a guest
on the Happy Sad Confused podcast, revealing

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:02.760
how he was so excited that he couldn't actually
take anything in.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.080
Grant admitted:

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:08.640
"I'm sure [Abrams] was telling me in detail
what part I was playing and what the character

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.280
is called, I have no memory of that whatsoever.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:15.040
They kept saying, 'So you are gonna do this,
aren't you?' and I said, 'Of course I'm gonna

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:15.560
do this!'"

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:20.570
The most popular theory was that Grant would
be taking on the role of Grand Admiral Thrawn,

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:25.610
a popular villain reintroduced into the canon
in the third season of Star Wars Rebels, but

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:29.300
the actor outright debunked that rumor when
Radio Times asked him about it.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.590
Grant dished, quote, "I'm not playing the
Star Wars character you just mentioned."

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.760
And he wasn't lying!

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:40.800
When Vanity Fair released a huge Episode IX
cover story in May 2019, the identity of Grant's

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:45.860
character was finally revealed, he's playing
a new villain named Allegiant General Pryde.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:51.260
Despite being thrown to what we thought was
certain death by a remorseful Anakin Skywalker

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:55.200
in 1983's Return of the Jedi, Emperor Palpatine
lives.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:59.400
At least, that's what Abrams seemed to suggest
with the first Episode IX teaser.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:03.760
The footage ends with a shot of some Death
Star wreckage and Palpatine's unmistakable

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:08.170
cackle, implying that our heroes will face
off against the powerful Sith in The Rise

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:09.160
of Skywalker.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:14.540
As if to confirm this was the case, Palpatine
actor Ian McDiarmid appeared onstage at Star

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.970
Wars Celebration 2019 during the teaser reveal.

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:22.140
"This was such an unexpected moment."

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:22.880
"I know!

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:23.520
It shocked me."

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:28.040
But how will Abrams explain his way out of
this one?

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.940
Theory crafters already have a few different
ideas.

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:36.760
MovieWeb reminded readers that, in the prequel
films, Palpatine has referenced Darth Plagueis,

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.960
a Sith lord so powerful and wise…

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.770
"…he could use the Force to influence the
midichlorians to create life."

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:48.020
Alternatively, the site argued, the Emperor
might use a loophole introduced in Star Wars

00:13:48.029 --> 00:13:52.260
Rebels: The so-called "World Between Worlds
in the hidden Jedi Temple on Lothal."

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:56.950
Apparently, Palpatine, quote, "sought to manipulate
[it] as he could travel through time by using

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:57.640
the Force."

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:02.420
Elsewhere, IGN believes that Abrams might
actually be taking some inspiration from an

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:03.960
Expanded Universe comic.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:09.120
In Dark Empire, Palpatine resurrects himself
several times via clones, transferring his

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.620
spirit to different bodies.

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:14.820
The first teaser for The Rise of Skywalker
gave theorists plenty to work with.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:19.200
Now that the Emperor's presence has been all
but confirmed, it's safe to assume that he'll

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.140
be involved in the film's final battle.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:26.080
Who, where, and how he'll be battling we don't
know for sure, but according to Making Star

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:31.440
Wars editor Jason Ward, there's a huge rumor
doing the rounds that pits Kylo Ren against

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:33.480
Palpatine, in the form of actor Matt Smith.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:33.980
Yup.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:34.640
This guy.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:35.780
This silly dude.

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:36.340
Right here.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:41.420
The British actor has been telling journalists
that he isn't in Episode IX, but that's contrary

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:42.400
to reports.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:47.500
Even international Disney websites are listing
the former Doctor Who star among the cast,

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.160
and Jason Ward believes that he'll play a
critical role.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:51.900
The mega fan reported:

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:55.620
"A really solid source over the years passed
on something they heard internally.

00:14:55.630 --> 00:15:01.180
The rumor is that Matt Smith isn't Palpatine
reborn or rejuvenated, but a dark side acolyte…During

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:06.860
the final act of the film Rey and Kylo team
up to fight the Palpatine possessed Matt Smith."

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:11.100
Ward's inside source claims that Kylo Ren
gets possessed by the Emperor after killing

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:14.000
his host body, leading to a moment of redemption.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:18.520
The tormented son of Han Solo and Leia Organa
has enough light left in him to lay down his

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:23.340
arms so Rey can finish the job, becoming Ben
Solo again in his final moments.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:28.160
With Kylo Ren dead, and Rey too pure for the
Emperor to possess, the fight is won.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:33.260
Most fans seemed pretty unhappy that The Last
Jedi neglected the Knights of Ren.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:38.120
Kylo Ren's band of warriors appear briefly
in The Force Awakens when Rey touches Luke

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:42.720
Skywalker's lightsaber and triggers a vision,
but they were left out of Rian Johnson's follow-up

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:46.100
because he, quote, "just didn't see a place
for them in the movie."

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:50.360
According to Vanity Fair, we're finally going
to get some answers in the upcoming trilogy-capper,

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:55.089
with sources at Disney confirming theories
that the, quote, "long-rumored Knights of

00:15:55.089 --> 00:15:57.320
Ren will finally arrive in Skywalker."

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:02.290
We got our first good look at the unit in
Annie Leibovitz's extensive photoshoot, and

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:05.880
what's immediately clear is that they're not
your typical Star Wars villains.

00:16:06.149 --> 00:16:10.420
In contrast to the sleek and shiny look adopted
by the First Order and the Galactic Empire

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:15.820
before it, the Knights of Ren wear dirty,
rag-tag armor and carry over-the-top weapons.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.960
Vanity Fair's Joanna Robinson observed:

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:23.020
"Their D.I.Y. look, including one especially
lethal-looking gun arm, would be equally at

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:25.040
home in one of the Mad Max movies."

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:29.220
Their identities have not yet been revealed,
though fans think they have a pretty good

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:30.900
idea about where they came from.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:35.800
In The Last Jedi, Luke reveals that Ren vanished
with a handful of his Padawan learners when

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.820
he set the temple ablaze and turned his back
on the Jedi.

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:41.500
Did Luke's former students become the Knights
of Ren?

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.860
Only time, as they say, will tell.

